PROVENANCE NOTE (added by OmniLink, 2026-08-22 — not part of the licence text)
=============================================================================

Package:  ur_description, version 4.3.1
Upstream: https://github.com/UniversalRobots/Universal_Robots_ROS2_Description
Licence:  BSD-3-Clause, as declared by upstream's own package.xml:
              <license file="LICENSE">BSD-3-Clause</license>
          (see projects/robots/universal_robots/ur_description/package.xml,
          shipped beside this file)

UNRESOLVED: THIS LICENCE HAS NO COPYRIGHT HOLDER OR YEAR.

The BSD-3 body below begins at "Redistribution and use..." with no
"Copyright (c) <year> <holder>" line above it. That is how upstream's own
LICENSE file is written; the line was not lost in transit here. It matters,
because BSD-3 clause 1 tells a redistributor to "retain the above copyright
notice" and there is no above copyright notice to retain, and clause 3 speaks
of "the name of the copyright holder" without the file ever naming one.

NO HOLDER OR YEAR IS ASSERTED HERE, because none could be established from
anything in this tree. What this tree does contain, and what it does not:

  * package.xml names Universal Robots A/S (ros@universal-robots.com) as a
    MAINTAINER, alongside maintainers Felix Exner and Rune Soe-Knudsen. A
    maintainer is not necessarily a copyright holder.
  * package.xml also lists sixteen AUTHOR entries -- Nadia Hammoudeh Garcia,
    Kelsey Hawkins, G.A. vd. Hoorn, Lovro Ivanov, Mathias Ludtke, Wim
    Meeussen, Felix Messmer, Miguel Prada Sarasola, Denis Stogl, Andy
    Zelenak, Marvin Grosse Besselmann, Tristan Schnell and Vincenzo Di
    Pentima among them -- i.e. the package has many contributors across
    several organisations, which is consistent with no single holder having
    been recorded.
  * The URDFs (urdf/ur3e.urdf, ur5e.urdf, ur10e.urdf) are xacro-generated and
    carry NO copyright header of any kind.
  * The visual meshes (meshes/ur{3e,5e,10e}/visual/*.dae) record only
    <author>Blender User</author> -- Blender's default author string, which
    names nobody -- with <authoring_tool>Blender 2.78.0</authoring_tool> and
    <created>2018-08-20</created>.
  * No README, NOTICE, AUTHORS or per-file copyright header exists anywhere
    in the package.

Anyone needing certainty should take the holder and year from upstream
directly rather than from this file, and should add the line here verbatim if
upstream ever records one. Guessing a holder would be worse than the gap.

SCOPE OF WHAT OMNISIM SHIPS: only the ur3e, ur5e and ur10e families, all of
which are BSD-3. Upstream places the UR8LONG / UR15 / UR18 / UR20 / UR30
meshes under Universal Robots A/S' separate "Terms and Conditions for Use of
Graphical Documentation" (package.xml declares that second licence, pointing
at meshes/ur20/LICENSE.txt). NONE of those families is redistributed here, and
that file is correspondingly absent. Do not add a restricted family without
re-checking those terms.

